  "id": "ajc-p1",
  "project": "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge",
  "projects": [
    "Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge"
  ],
  "title": "AJC prover p1: claim and close the 1st-most important representability item",
  "objective": "You are prover lane `ajc-p1` on Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge. This round the objective is deliberately FREE: nobody has told you which declaration to prove. Your objective is to identify the MOST important open item standing between this project and Picard/Pic^0 representability, claim it publicly, and discharge it.\n\nREAD FIRST: protection item `I-0838`. It is the claim protocol for this round's ten parallel lanes and it is not optional \u2014 steps 2 through 5 (check ownership, claim with `roadmap set --owner ajc-p1`, announce, release on exit) are what stop four lanes proving the same lemma. Also read `I-0491` and `I-0492`, the two binding human decisions, before touching the seam.\n\nYOUR RANK. You take the MOST important item. Rank is a tie-break so four lanes do not converge on one target, not a fence: if your item turns out to be blocked on another lane's, say so in the inbox and swap. On a contested item you first refusal on any contested item.\n\nYOUR PEERS this round are ajc-p1, ajc-p2, ajc-p3, ajc-p4 plus the reviewer `review-ajc`. The reviewer is auditing route and organisation and will be correcting the board in its first hour \u2014 read its inbox items before you fix your target, and re-read them if you are about to start something large. It may direct-message you a proposal; weigh it against what you hold, and take it if it is genuinely worth more. You may propose work to the other lanes the same way (`inbox add --kind hint --to task:<lane>`), naming declaration, file, and why it beats what they hold.\n\nHOW TO CHOOSE, since this is the part I am delegating to you. \"Most important\" means: measured against the project's representability headline, what does discharging this buy? A leaf that unblocks three others beats a leaf that is merely nearest. A leaf whose stated prerequisite turns out to already exist in the file beats both \u2014 earlier sessions' costings in this workspace have been wrong in that direction more than once, so read the actual Lean hypothesis, not the prose about it. Use `horizon graph -p Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge frontier` for the ranked view, `horizon roadmap list --focus AJC.picrep / AJC.jacobian` for the board, and `horizon search` (which spans both projects AND mathlib) before you prove anything \u2014 the premise you need is often already next door under a name you would not have grepped.\n\nTHE BAR, and it is higher than usual this round. An audit on 2026-07-29 sampled 101 representability claims across both projects and refuted 99: 67 were sorry-reachable, 17 VACUOUS, 12 proved something adjacent to what they claimed, 3 did not exist. So:\n- Sorry-free is necessary, not sufficient. Before you report a gate closed, exhibit a witness for EVERY antecedent, or state plainly which antecedent remains undischarged. \"The implication is proved\" and \"the conclusion holds for some curve\" are different claims and I want to know which you have.\n- Never introduce a class, structure field, or side condition whose statement does not mention the object it is about. The cautionary case is `HasDivFunctor`: its field asserted only that a presheaf category is nonempty, the curve did not occur, and the blueprint advertised it as the existence of the divisor functor with `\\leanok`. It survived because nobody read the statement.\n- Never discharge an obligation by projecting the hypothesis you assumed. `choose_spec.1` of your own binder is `P \u2192 P`.\n- A green build is not evidence of non-vacuity, and `lean_multi_attempt` reports every snippet as closing the goal when the file's imports are stale. Check imports before believing a probe.\n- Do not restate an obligation more weakly to make a count go down. If you cannot close it, leave it open and say why.\n\nONE SHARED LEDGER, ten writers. Another lane's integrate sweep can commit your half-written file before you have measured it once \u2014 write risky proofs as explicit `sorry` first, measure, then fill. Stage explicit files, never `add -A`. Commit at every coherent point; an interrupted lane loses only what was uncommitted. Follow the `lean-check` LSP loop for edits and keep `lake build` for the session boundary \u2014 nine other lanes want the build lock too.\n\nWHERE THIS PROJECT ACTUALLY STANDS, so you do not rediscover it. The entire Jacobian tower rests on ONE bare `sorry`: `fgaPicardRepresentability` at `AlgebraicJacobian/Picard/FGAPicRepresentability.lean:347`. Its unique consumer chain runs through `instHasPicSchemeEt` (an unconditional producer that is a projection of that sorry) to the headline. The legacy `HasPicScheme` class has NO instance, so the ~45 declarations taking `[HasPicScheme C]` currently prove nothing about any curve. `instPicSharpRepresentable` and `instPicSchemeLocallyOfFiniteType` are `choose_spec` projections of their own hypothesis. `smoothProperQuotient` proves `P.IsRepresentable \u2192 P.IsRepresentable` with all four Kleiman hypotheses unused and zero call sites. `HasDivFunctor` is vacuous as described above.\n\nThe line-347 docstring says discharging it needs Kleiman \u00a74 \u2014 the Abel-map slice `Div^d \u2192 Pic^d` as a smooth proper equivalence relation with scheme quotient, plus `Div` representability via Quot \u2014 while the board marks BOTH `AJC.picrep.quot` and `AJC.picrep.serre` `rejected`. That contradiction is the reviewer's first assignment; if it resolves before you fix your target, use its answer.\n\nBoard caveat: `AJC.picrep` is marked `done` and its advertised deliverable `instHasPicScheme` exists in no `.lean` file \u2014 deleted 2026-07-28 under `I-0491`, not discharged. Do not read `done` on that subtree as truth until the reviewer has corrected it. Open non-done items you might weigh: `AJC.picrep.tensor` (pullback-tensor and fibre base change), `AJC.rr.extuniform` (extension-uniform H1 vanishing, one threshold serving every fibre), `AJC.fbc.cosimplicial.twisted` (the twisted \u010cech nerve naturality square that separates this project from Stacks 02KH), `AJC.pic0av.tangent` / `.structure` / `.identity`, `AJC.albanese.symmetric` / `.universal`. Body-position sorries live in `Albanese/AlbaneseUP.lean` (6), `Jacobian.lean` (4), `Picard/Pic0AbelianVariety.lean` (3), `Picard/SerreFiniteness.lean` (2), `Picard/QuotFunctorDef.lean` (2), `Picard/Pic0Et.lean` (2), `Picard/IdentityComponent.lean` (2), `Picard/QuotRepresentability.lean` (1), `FGAPicRepresentability.lean` (1), `Cohomology/CechHigherDirectImageUnconditional.lean` (1).\n\nA real option, and I want you to consider it seriously rather than defaulting to a leaf: the sibling project Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge-Rebuild has a genuinely sorry-free representability engine (`pic0RepresentableByOfCharts`, `Picard/Pic0SigmaSheaf.lean:161`) whose inputs are chart data rather than Quot. `horizon search` spans both projects. If AJC's route is blocked on Quot and the sibling's is not, the highest-value thing a lane can do here may be to import or transcribe that route rather than push on Kleiman \u00a74. Price it before you commit to it \u2014 a cross-project object-level match can be true and still irrelevant if the carrier the statement binds differs.\n\nWHAT I WANT AT THE END. Your report should answer three things without me having to ask: which item you claimed and why it was the most important one, what its state is now (closed sorry-free with all antecedents witnessed / closed as an implication with named antecedents still open / advanced with the remaining obligation stated / blocked, with the blocker), and what you learned that changes another lane's plan. If you found a costing wrong, a vacuity, or a route problem, that goes in the inbox as an `issue` at the site that made the claim \u2014 not only in your report, which nobody downstream reads.\n\nIf your first-choice item collapses on inspection \u2014 the prerequisite already exists, or the statement turns out vacuous, or another lane got there first \u2014 that is a finding, not a wasted session. Record it, release the claim, and take the next item. Do not sit on a claimed item you are not working.",
